; Pure-OCaml native inference engine (no libtorch / ctypes). Built bottom-up per
; .ai/native_inference_design.md; storage is Bigarray. `wrapped false` is the repo
; convention, so modules are referenced unqualified (Axis, Dim, Vec6, …).

(include_subdirs unqualified)

; Two profile-gated stanzas, not one library with an always-on ppx: measured
; `landmarks-ppx --auto`-instrumented lib/native at ~2.3x slower
; (6.1s -> 14.4s on the conv2d benchmark) than uninstrumented, even with
; profiling never started — the ppx's per-function instrumentation has real
; cost on this codebase even when idle, unlike e.g. memtrace's env-gated
; `trace_if_requested`. So the instrumented build has to be a separate
; artifact, never the one `benchmark.native_conv2d`/tests/every other
; consumer links against. `dune build --profile landmarks` selects the
; instrumented stanza; plain `dune build` (any other profile) gets the
; uninstrumented one, identical to before this split. bin/dune's
; `aten_spec_verify` executable needs no matching split itself — it
; unconditionally links `landmarks` and self-gates *starting* profiling on
; an env var, same idiom as memtrace; see the comment there. See
; .ai/pt2_inference_perf.md's landmarks section.

(library
 (name native)
 (enabled_if
  (<> %{profile} landmarks))
 (libraries core expr fmt jsont jsont.bytesrw walk_core)
 (wrapped false))

(library
 (name native)
 (enabled_if
  (= %{profile} landmarks))
 (libraries core expr fmt jsont jsont.bytesrw walk_core landmarks)
 (preprocess
  (pps landmarks-ppx --auto))
 (wrapped false))
